SE_P = 'Subthreshold analog front-ends operating at I<sub>D</sub> = 8–95 nA (g<sub>m</sub>/I<sub>D</sub> ≈ 25–27 V⁻¹) exhibit exponential sensitivity to threshold voltage V<sub>th</sub>, thermal voltage U<sub>T</sub> = kT/q, and positive-feedback capacitor ratios β<sub>IBL</sub> = C<sub>pf</sub>/C<sub>fb</sub>. Using <b>Cadence Spectre</b> (`sm141064.scs`) and <b>Synopsys HSPICE</b> (`sm141064.hspice`, including native `.sens` + `.alter` sweeps) across all <b>36 deliverable ECG front-end cards</b> on the compute farm, we quantify the normalized sensitivity S<sup>Y</sup><sub>p</sub> and 3σ physical variation impact of all 10 variation sources to guide the exact bit-width, LSB step size, and tuning range of on-chip calibration cells.'

